/T (large.example has 50 sub-domains: 42 in-scope hosts and 8 CNAMEs pointing at a third-partySaaS vendor. The original strategy queried A, AAAA, MX, TXT and CNAME for everycandidate \(77 wordlist names plus 38 passive-seed names, not de-duplicated\) and followedCNAMEs into vendor space. The modified strategy de-duplicates first, sends one A queryper candidate, records CNAME targets without following them, and makes one AXFRattempt and one apex TXT query. )
/E (large.example has 50 sub-domains: 42 in-scope hosts and 8 CNAMEs pointing at a third-partySaaS vendor. The original strategy queried A, AAAA, MX, TXT and CNAME for everycandidate \(77 wordlist names plus 38 passive-seed names, not de-duplicated\) and followedCNAMEs into vendor space. The modified strategy de-duplicates first, sends one A queryper candidate, records CNAME targets without following them, and makes one AXFRattempt and one apex TXT query. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [33]
>>
