/T (Handling rules. Verified in-scope findings go into thereport. Unverified items are held in a re-check list. Out-of-scope items are logged as boundary notes with zero probes. Personal data \(the two e-mail addresses and one name found\) is masked in the report \(e.g. it-a***@leaky.example\) and never used for contact. Treating all of these alike would have inflated leaky.example by 2 phantom hosts and stale.example by 2 phantom hosts and 1 out-of-scope probe. )
