/T (versus 75 %\) because the fixed discovery cost dominates; the original gives full-depth data on 100 % of hosts at trivial cost. \(2\) Teaching, where uniform depth is easier to explain and trace. \(3\) A required full service inventory or a compliance scan, where the sampling rule would drop detail. \(4\) IPv6 zones, where the AAAA-sampling shortcut was not tested and could hide records if the sample is unrepresentative. )
/E (versus 75 %\) because the fixed discovery cost dominates; the original gives full-depth data on 100 % of hosts at trivial cost. \(2\) Teaching, where uniform depth is easier to explain and trace. \(3\) A required full service inventory or a compliance scan, where the sampling rule would drop detail. \(4\) IPv6 zones, where the AAAA-sampling shortcut was not tested and could hide records if the sample is unrepresentative. )
